# Specify files that shouldn't be modified by Fern
# All of .github/ is ours, so Fern can't add, change or remove a workflow, including the release one:
# our own CI (GitHub-hosted runners, pinned actions, no publish job; see ci.yml's header), the manifest check
# (changes need the dependencies-approved label) and CODEOWNERS (Enterprise owns the whole repo).
.github/
# Secret and internal-reference checks for local commits; CI's secrets job runs the same ones.
.gitleaks.toml
.pre-commit-config.yaml
# Default base URL is exactly https://developers.synthesia.io.
tests/custom/baseUrl.test.ts
# Same LICENSE (MIT) and SECURITY.md as the other synthesia-ai repos. Fern's Python LICENSE names the package, not
# Synthesia, as the copyright holder, and its TypeScript generator writes none.
LICENSE
SECURITY.md
# Fern's CONTRIBUTING.md sends SDK questions to Fern's own issue tracker and invites pull requests we don't take.
CONTRIBUTING.md
